# One gust front crossing grass, then a bush, then a tree crown
# (src/render/wind.gdshaderinc gust_at; grass.gdshader and world.gdshader's
# sward sheen; leaf.gdshader, where a gust turns the leaves pale side up).
#   tools/tour.sh tours/foliage_front.tour --seed=7
# `near front` (18_trample) finds a bush in grass with a crown downwind of it on
# the world's wind line and stands the player beside that line, so from above
# the frame holds the grass upwind, the bush, and the crown mid-frame; the log
# prints where both are. A full held wind carries a band about 6 tiles a second
# and a band is about 7 tiles deep, so frames 0.75 s apart (01-04, 2.25 s in
# all) watch one band come over the grass, the bush and the crown in turn.
# 05-06 over the shoulder, 1.5 s apart.
weather clear:0:wind=1
hour 11
coast calm
place coast
near front
zoom 9
wait 2.0
shot 01-front-from-above with land:coast,prop:bush
wait 0.75
shot 02-front-0.75s-on with land:coast,prop:bush
wait 0.75
shot 03-front-1.5s-on with land:coast,prop:bush
wait 0.75
shot 04-front-2.25s-on with land:coast,prop:bush
zoom 12
hold shoulder_peek
await shoulder 3
wait 1.0
shot 05-front-over-the-shoulder with land:coast
wait 1.5
shot 06-front-over-the-shoulder-1.5s-on with land:coast
release shoulder_peek
weather rules
